  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "It is important to note that confusion about gender identity is a normal part of the process of coming to terms with one's gender identity. It is important to provide support and understanding to the individual, and to encourage them to seek professional help if they are struggling with their gender identity. Some warning signs that may indicate confusion about gender identity include:\n\n  * Difficulty with gender expression or identity\n  * Confusion about their own gender identity\n  * Difficulty with gender roles or expectations\n  * Difficulty with gender-based discrimination or harassment\n  * Difficulty with gender-based violence or abuse\n  * Difficulty with gender-based mental health issues, such as depression or anxiety.\n\nIt is important to remember that confusion about gender identity is a normal part of the process of coming to terms with one's gender identity, and that seeking professional help is a sign of strength, not weakness. If you are concerned about someone's confusion about gender identity, it is important to provide support and understanding, and to encourage them to seek professional help if they are struggling.",
